<article class="env-lemma" id="02N4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02N4">Lemma <span data-tag="02N4">17.20.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a flat morphism of ringed spaces. Then the pullback functor $f^* : \textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ Y) \to \textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ is exact. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The functor $f^*$ is the composition of the exact functor $f^{-1} : \textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ Y) \to \textit{Mod}(f^{-1}\mathcal{O}_ Y)$ and the change of rings functor 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \textit{Mod}(f^{-1}\mathcal{O}_ Y) \to \textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ X), \quad \mathcal{F} \longmapsto \mathcal{F} \otimes _{f^{-1}\mathcal{O}_ Y} \mathcal{O}_ X.  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Thus the result follows from the discussion following Definition <a href="/tag/02N3" data-tag="02N3">17.20.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>